          "lem-normal-density-has-total-mass-one",
          "thm-linear-change-of-variables-for-lebesgue-measure",
          "thm-linearity-of-the-lebesgue-integral-on-l-one"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 5
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-finite-priors-approximate-gaussian-shift-bayes-risk",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Finite priors approximate Gaussian-shift Bayes values",
        "statement": "Assume AC. Let $Q_h=N_d(h,S)$ with $S\\succ0$ and let $g:\\mathbb R^d\\to[0,M]$ have Lipschitz constant $B<\\infty$. For every Borel probability prior $\\pi$ on $\\mathbb R^d$ and $\\epsilon>0$, there is a finite-support prior $\\pi_f$ whose Bayes value for loss $g(a-h)$ differs from that of $\\pi$ by less than $\\epsilon$. The comparison is uniform over all measurable randomized rules. In particular this applies to every diffuse Gaussian prior; no posterior selector assumption is needed.",
        "deps": [
          "def-bayes-and-minimax-risk",
          "def-measure-kernel-and-probability-kernel",
          "def-multivariate-normal-law",
          "def-total-variation-distance-for-probability-laws",
