          "lem-bowl-shaped-loss-has-centered-lipschitz-minorants",
          "lem-finite-prior-lan-bayes-envelope-convergence",
          "lem-finite-priors-approximate-gaussian-shift-bayes-risk",
          "def-multivariate-normal-law",
          "def-standard-normal-and-normal-laws",
          "lem-normal-density-has-total-mass-one",
          "thm-linear-change-of-variables-for-lebesgue-measure",
          "thm-cauchy-schwarz-and-the-euclidean-norm",
          "def-axiom-of-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "statement": "Assume AC. Let $\\{P_{n,h}:h\\in\\mathbb R^d\\}$ be a pointwise LAN experiment in the sense of [[def-lan-experiment]], with positive-definite information matrix $K$. Let $L:\\mathbb R^d\\to[0,M]$ be Borel measurable, symmetric and quasi-convex. Then\n$$\\liminf_{c\\to\\infty}\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}\\inf_{\\widehat h_n}\\sup_{\\|h\\|_2\\le c}E_{P_{n,h}}L(\\widehat h_n-h)\\ge E L(Z),\\qquad Z\\sim N_d(0,K^{-1}).$$\nThe infimum includes every measurable randomized estimator. Only pointwise LAN at each fixed local parameter is required: no compact-uniform likelihood approximation, joint parameter likelihood field or posterior selector assumption is imposed."
      },
